    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Plants have several different photosynthetic pigments in their chloroplasts.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6
        }
      }
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "label": "(a)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 6
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A student separated and identified the chloroplast pigments present in a leaf extract from a spinach plant using two slightly different methods.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method <b>A</b>",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "A type of chromatography known as thin layer chromatography (TLC) was used to separate the pigments.",
              "A mixture of ether and cyclohexane was used as a solvent in TLC."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method <b>B</b>",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "The student repeated TLC but treated the spinach leaf extract with a chemical. The chemical causes a magnesium ion in a pigment to be replaced by two hydrogen ions.",
              "The student used a leaf from the same spinach plant, and used the same solvent as in method <b>A</b>."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The student calculated R<sub>f</sub> values and compared these to reference values to identify the pigments.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 3.1 shows the results for method <b>A</b> and method <b>B</b>.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig3.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 3.1",
            "src": "figures/q3_fig3_1.png",
            "alt": "Two chromatography methods",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "parts": [
