      {
        "key": "c",
        "label": "(c)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 9,
          "ms": 11
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In some species of plant, the absorption of light stimulates seed germination.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The absorption of light increases the production of gibberellin in the embryo of a seed.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Describe the role of gibberellin in the germination of a seed.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 4,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "15.2(3)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 4,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>four</i></b><i> from</i>:",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "<b>1</b>    gibberellin, moves to / acts on / stimulates, <u>aleurone</u> layer<b> ; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "<b>2 </b> <b> </b> binds to, (gibberellin) receptor / GID(1)<b> ; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "<b>3 </b> <b> </b> breaks down <u>DELLA</u> (protein)<b> ; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "<b>4 </b> <b> </b> releases, PIF / transcription factor <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "<b>5 </b> <b> </b> switches on <u>gene</u> for, amylase / maltase / protease <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "text": "<b>6</b>    amylase, breaks down / hydrolyses, starch to maltose <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "text": "<b>7</b>    sugars / glucose, for, respiration / growth, of embryo<b> ; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Gibberellin from the embryo stimulates the aleurone layer to produce hydrolytic enzymes. Digestion mobilises reserves for growth before the seedling can photosynthesise sufficiently.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:15.2(3)",
                "ms:c#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Distinguish the hormone source from the responding tissue.",
            "Connect enzyme production to mobilisation of food reserves."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Saying that gibberellin itself hydrolyses starch",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:15.2(3)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
      }
